<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huế</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hue, Phu Xuan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huế, formerly Phu Xuan, is a city on the Perfume River in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. It became the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyen lords</a> in the 17th and 18th centuries and was captured by the Tay Son. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gia-long">Nguyen Anh</a> retook it in 1801, it was the imperial capital of the Nguyen dynasty until 1945, and its citadel is a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hue.jpg" alt="Huế" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lê Huy Hoàng Hải · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Th%C3%A0nh_ph%E1%BB%91_Hu%E1%BA%BF_nh%C3%ACn_t%E1%BB%AB_tr%C3%AAn_cao_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
